title: Friends on the Executive
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and lw_court_timer <= 0 and comintern_member = 1 and time >= 6
on-arrival: {!
Q.lw_court_timer = 6;
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.lw_court_played = (Q.lw_court_played || 0) + 1;
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.card();
!}
frequency: 130
is-card: true
tags: international

= Friends on the Executive

The Executive of the International is five men, and each of them reads the German reports for something different. A party that wants to be heard in Moscow needs a friend there; a party that has none will be spoken about, not spoken to.

The Zentrale's representative in Moscow asks whose door he should knock on this month. [? if ecci_friend_name : Our best friend there is said to be [+ ecci_friend_name +]. ?] [? if directive_active = 1 : The directive from [+ directive_from_name +] is still open. ?]

- @lenin: Send Lenin the facts he always asks for.
- @zinoviev: Pledge discipline to Zinoviev.
- @radek: Share the Berlin gossip with Radek.
- @bukharin: Ask Bukharin to write for the German party.
- @trotsky: Send Trotsky a report on the Reichswehr.
- @easy_discard

@lenin
subtitle: A long report on wages, prices and the unions. Lenin is pleased; the others notice he is the one who was asked.
view-if: ecci_lenin_ill = 0
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('lenin', 10);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -2);
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 2);
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 1, 1);
!}

The report runs to sixty pages, with tables. It comes back with pencil marks in the margins, and one note at the end: "Good. More of this."

@zinoviev
subtitle: The President likes obedience. Zinoviev is pleased; our independence suffers, and the Left is encouraged.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 10);
Q.independence -= 4;
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 1, 2);
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 0, -2);
!}

The Zentrale's letter to the President promises iron discipline, the unconditional application of the Executive's decisions and the struggle against every deviation. It is a letter Zinoviev likes to read aloud.

@radek
subtitle: Radek likes to know everything first. He is pleased; something may leak the other way.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('radek', 10);
if (Math.random() < 0.3) { Q.lw_out = 1; Q.unity -= 3; }
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 1, 2);
!}

Our man in Moscow spends an evening with Radek and tells him who said what at the last three meetings of the Zentrale. [? if lw_out = 1 : A month later, half of it is repeated at a session of the Executive, with names, and the German comrades concerned are not amused. ?][? if lw_out = 0 : Radek laughs a great deal, and promises to put in a word. ?]

@bukharin
subtitle: An article from Bukharin for the party press. He is flattered; the theory of the offensive comes with it.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('bukharin', 9);
Q.militancy += 2;
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 1, 3);
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 0, -2);
!}

Bukharin writes for the German party within a week: twelve pages on the German revolution, which he has never seen, and which he describes very vividly.

@trotsky
subtitle: The Commissar for War values hard information. Trotsky is pleased; the police would be very interested.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('trotsky', 9);
Q.red_guards_arms += 1;
Q.repression += 1;
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 1, 1);
!}

The report lists the Reichswehr's garrisons, its secret reserves and the names of officers who drink too much. Trotsky sends back a short letter of thanks and a longer list of questions.
